'''VRDancing''' is a PC-only dance studio [[Special:MyLanguage/:Category:Worlds|world]] where players follow choreography videos from a searchable in-world database of over 13,000 entries.<ref name="listing">[https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_42377cf1-c54f-45ed-8996-5875b0573a83 VRDancing] on ''vrchat.com''.</ref>

== Layout ==

Players spawn in a changing room. A rules-agreement panel sits at the exit. The room has avatar lockers, a mirror with announcements, a story desk, and a Patreon bench. Lockers include Echo by TinkerLucy (v5.0.0). Kytö by Sohvi is the first official VRDancing furry avatar (v5.6.0). The story desk shows write-ups from community members.

The dance floor can be small or large. The main video player is on the floor. A database and queue appear when approached. Bleachers face the floor. A door leads to a garden. The Marshall Shrine and an upstairs TV are in the world. Donation-progress displays sit in the changing room and on the dance floor.<ref name="world">[https://www.vrdancing.club/world Worlds] on ''vrdancing.club''.</ref>

== Features ==

The database is searchable and filterable. Players can create up to five persistent custom tags. Video previews were added in v5.9.0 on {{Date|2025-12-04}}.

A queue holds upcoming videos. It has vote skip, playlist export, and playlist import.

Settings, camera setups, and video history persist with [[Special:MyLanguage/Persistence|Persistence]]. Instance history keeps the last 100 videos. Persistent history keeps the last 500. The default video player is AVPro. Players can switch to UnityVideoPlayer. The servers are VRD-CDN and VRD-CDN-LQ (v5.3.0, {{Date|2025-08-14}}). Switch Server is on the database and in the options menu. ALT+P fullscreens the video on desktop.

Camera modes are Follow, Static, Animated, and Handheld. Staff can hand out microphones as of v5.4.0.<ref name="world" />

== Community ==

VRDancing hosts weekly dance, fitness, and hangout events in EU, NA, and Asia-Pacific. Full-body tracking is not required. Weekend sessions run on Saturdays. A community instructor curates the playlist. Open sessions run on Wednesdays. Anyone in the instance can queue a choreography. Weekend times are {{Time|21:00}} CET and {{Time|19:00}} CST. Open session times are {{Time|20:00}} CET, {{Time|19:00}} CST, and {{Time|19:00}} JST.<ref name="home">[https://www.vrdancing.club/ VRDancing] on ''vrdancing.club''.</ref> Events are not Meta Quest compatible.<ref name="join">[https://www.vrdancing.club/join How to join] on ''vrdancing.club''.</ref> The [[Special:MyLanguage/Groups|VRChat group]] is [https://vrchat.com/home/group/grp_d960be54-cfc2-44cb-863d-6d624d8975c1 VRDancing] (VRD.9523).

Experience points (XP) are tracked on Discord. XP is awarded only after the Discord command <code>/setmyname</code> links a VRChat display name. Leaving Discord removes the rank. The rank returns after enough XP for the next rank. Ranks are Discord roles.<ref name="discord">[https://discord.gg/VRDancing VRDancing Discord]. Levels {{Date|2022-09-16}}; Marshallthon {{Date|2021-08-02}} and {{Date|2022-07-26}}.</ref> The command <code>/setdisplayrank</code> sets the displayed role to any rank already earned. It does not change XP or the actual rank. A level-up assigns the new rank.<ref name="displayrank">[https://www.vrdancing.club/announcements/discord-bot-change-your-name-color-update Discord bot: change your name color] on ''vrdancing.club''.</ref>

Weekend and open sessions award XP from a button at the end of the event. XP from those sessions is credited at the end of the week. The cap is 10 XP per week. Weekend session instructors earn an extra 20 XP. A dance video submitted on Discord awards 20 XP once per calendar month. The video must be at least one minute. The same choreography cannot be submitted twice. Officer (150 XP) unlocks Discord submissions to the story desk.<ref name="discord" />

